## 🗒️ Reflections / Notes
This incident highlights the critical danger of operating with unconfigured network perimeter defenses. Relying on firewalls without active rules leaves an organization completely vulnerable to automated, high-volume threats like ICMP floods, turning what should be a minor event into a full operational shutdown. 

Moving forward, our cybersecurity strategy must transition from a reactive model to a proactive, layered defense-in-depth approach. Implementing the NIST CSF functions ensures that we do not just block the immediate attack, but also continuously monitor our baselines, automate our response capabilities, and establish reliable communication protocols. For a multimedia company serving small businesses, maintaining network availability is directly tied to client trust and business reputation; therefore, regular architecture audits and infrastructure hardening must be treated as continuous business-critical processes rather than one-time technical tasks.

